<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Regression Results by Subject</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A1.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ Appendix A Regression Results by Subject ‣ The Token Tax: Systematic Bias in Multilingual Tokenization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A1.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Appendix A Regression Results by Subject ‣ The Token Tax: Systematic Bias in Multilingual Tokenization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> show results of accuracy-on-fertility regressions for the 10 models over 5 subjects.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.05486v1/figures/all_models_combined_grid_subplots.png" id="A1.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" style="aspect-ratio:333/666;" width="333" height="666" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 3</span>: </span><span id="A1.F3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fertility vs. accuracy trade-offs for the 10 models across five MMLU subjects including correlation coefficient.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 1</span>: </span><span id="A1.T1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Fertility vs Accuracy by Model and Subject. Results from linear models regressing accuracy on translation fertility across 16 languages for each model-subject combination. Negative slopes indicate that higher fertility (more diverse translations) correlates with lower accuracy. Bold p-values indicate statistical significance (p <math id="A1.T1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>). Asterisks (*) indicate results that remain significant after Benjamini-Hochberg FDR correction (FDR <math id="A1.T1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;0.05</annotation></semantics></math>). Bold <math id="A1.T1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> values indicate correlations with large effect sizes (<math id="A1.T1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\rho|\geq 0.50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0.50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\rho|\geq 0.50</annotation></semantics></math>). <math id="A1.T1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> values show the proportion of variance in accuracy explained by fertility and bold text indicates large effect sizes by Cohen’s convention (<math id="A1.T1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A1.T1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≥</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq</annotation></semantics></math> 0.25). Regressions for o1 are not included because Openai has not released details on the tokenizer for this model.</span></figcaption>
